      "category": "control mismatch",
      "finding": "The flat arm is not shown to differ only in the metric. It uses a different projection radius (0.99 versus (1-1e-5)/sqrt(0.1), approximately 3.162), so the feasible representation region and projection behavior differ substantially. It also uses identity map instead of the curved arm's exponential map (even though the curved arm's map approaches identity as c tends to zero), and the fixed R=0.99 exception is not the limit of the curved arm's stated R(c). These are changes in representation/projection, not merely the distance metric.",
